close_reason: Non-record history lines refuse with a typed error and salvage recovers them
contract_change:
  api: History stream readers and pm history-repair --salvage-tail
  before: "A history line that was valid JSON but not an object crashed pm activity, pm context, pm history and pm get with unknown_error, and --salvage-tail refused a line holding a JSON null, boolean or number"
  after: "Every reader refuses such a line with history_record_invalid naming item_id, reason and details.line; --salvage-tail removes JSON null, boolean and number lines wherever they sit, reports non_record_lines in its receipt, and still refuses strings, arrays and incomplete objects"
  migrate: "Branch on history_record_invalid instead of unknown_error and follow its next step, pm history-repair <id> --salvage-tail --dry-run"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_added
  owner: pm-jbplbq
  gate_id: history-record-invalid-refusal
  negative_control: "tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts appends a JSON null, number, boolean, string and array line to a stream. For each it asserts that readHistoryEntries and the activity, context and history commands refuse with history_record_invalid (item_id, reason, details.line) and never unknown_error, and that --salvage-tail recovers a scalar line even after a later pm write. tests/integration/history-durability.integration.spec.ts asserts that salvage still refuses strings, arrays and incomplete objects."
  local_checks[1]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts tests/integration/history-durability.integration.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.spec.ts
  hosted_checks[2]: CI / Gates (static),CI / Gates (coverage)
